WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.150
Methanal.

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.830
Ethanoic acid.

3
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.030
Glucose.

4
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.830
Three substances that
behave nothing alike.

5
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.050
Analyse each one for
carbon, hydrogen and oxygen,

6
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.970
and work out a formula from the results.

7
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.570
All three come out the same: CH₂O.

8
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.510
Three different substances, one formula.

9
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.930
How can that be?

10
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.930
In this mission, you'll turn
percentages by mass into a formula,

11
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.750
one step at a time, starting
from a 100 gram sample.

12
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.650
You'll meet two kinds of formula,

13
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.430
empirical and molecular,
and learn to calculate both.

14
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.160
Your mission: explain how three different
substances can share one formula.
